          "note": "Riffian ⟨c⟩ = [ʃ]. Wiktionary writes the palatalized velar as *ḱ (Kossmann's *kʲ, also cited as *c); geminate *kk stays kk (kkes 'take off'), and singleton plain *k follows a separate spirantization path, while Kabyle and Tashelhit merge *kʲ with k (akal, krez). The Zenati shift has a fair number of irregular correspondences: Mzab keeps aker 'steal'."
